<template>
  <j-page class="store-page detail-page">
    <main>
      <nav class="breadcrumb-line" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" data-jv-router>Catalog</a>
        <j-icon name="chevron_right" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
        <span>Databases</span>
        <j-icon name="chevron_right" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
        <strong>MySQL</strong>
      </nav>

      <section class="detail-hero" aria-labelledby="mysql-title">
        <span class="package-icon package-icon--mysql package-icon--large" aria-hidden="true">
          <j-icon name="database"></j-icon>
        </span>
        <div class="detail-hero__copy">
          <div class="package-badges">
            <j-badge class="trust-badge">
              <j-icon name="verified" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
              Official
            </j-badge>
            <j-badge class="preview-badge">Source kit</j-badge>
          </div>
          <h1 id="mysql-title">MySQL</h1>
          <p>Stateful MySQL 8.4 with fenced storage, secret delivery, health checks, resource limits, and an operator-tested restore path.</p>
          <div class="fact-strip" aria-label="Package facts">
            <span><j-icon name="tag" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>nextera/mysql · 8.4</span>
            <span><j-icon name="license" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>GPL-2.0-only</span>
            <span><j-icon name="developer_board" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>amd64 / arm64</span>
            <span><j-icon name="devices" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Linux · ChromeOS · macOS · Windows clients</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <j-alert class="readiness-alert">
        <j-icon name="info" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
        <div>
          <strong>This is a reviewed source kit, not a registry release.</strong>
          <p>The immutable package digest, publisher signature, SBOM, and install evidence will appear here after the publishing pipeline is live.</p>
        </div>
      </j-alert>

      <div class="detail-layout">
        <section class="detail-content" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
          <j-card class="detail-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Operational design</span>
              <h2 id="overview-title">What this kit protects</h2>
              <p>The database files live on a NexRun volume with an exclusive fenced lease, not in the container's writable layer. Restart, redeploy, and daemon recovery preserve the data while the fencing epoch prevents a stale second writer.</p>
              <ul class="feature-list">
                <li><j-icon name="check_circle" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><span>MySQL 8.4 OCI runtime</span></li>
                <li><j-icon name="check_circle" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><span>Required root password delivered as a scoped secret file</span></li>
                <li><j-icon name="check_circle" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><span>Readiness through <code>mysqladmin ping</code></span></li>
                <li><j-icon name="check_circle" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><span>Graceful 60-second termination period</span></li>
                <li><j-icon name="check_circle" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><span>Snapshot, logical, and point-in-time recovery guidance</span></li>
              </ul>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>

          <j-card class="detail-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Current source-kit flow</span>
              <h2>Review before deployment</h2>
              <j-list class="install-list">
                <j-list-item>
                  <j-item-section class="step-number">1</j-item-section>
                  <j-item-section>
                    <j-item-label>Install and inspect NexRun</j-item-label>
                    <j-item-label>Run <code>nexrun doctor</code> on the target Linux runtime.</j-item-label>
                  </j-item-section>
                </j-list-item>
                <j-list-item>
                  <j-item-section class="step-number">2</j-item-section>
                  <j-item-section>
                    <j-item-label>Prepare storage and configuration</j-item-label>
                    <j-item-label>Create the data and configuration volumes, then place <code>my.cnf</code> on the read-only configuration volume.</j-item-label>
                  </j-item-section>
                </j-list-item>
                <j-list-item>
                  <j-item-section class="step-number">3</j-item-section>
                  <j-item-section>
                    <j-item-label>Create the scoped secret</j-item-label>
                    <j-item-label>Use NexRun secret tooling to create <code>mysql-root-password</code>; never place it in the manifest.</j-item-label>
                  </j-item-section>
                </j-list-item>
                <j-list-item>
                  <j-item-section class="step-number">4</j-item-section>
                  <j-item-section>
                    <j-item-label>Validate and deploy</j-item-label>
                    <j-item-label>Validate the IDEL workload locally before changing runtime state.</j-item-label>
                  </j-item-section>
                </j-list-item>
                <j-list-item>
                  <j-item-section class="step-number">5</j-item-section>
                  <j-item-section>
                    <j-item-label>Complete a restore drill</j-item-label>
                    <j-item-label>Retain measured RPO/RTO and restore evidence before production use.</j-item-label>
                  </j-item-section>
                </j-list-item>
              </j-list>
              <div class="command-block">
                <div class="command-block__bar">
                  <j-icon name="terminal" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
                  bash
                  <em>run on the target host</em>
                </div>
                <pre><code><span class="cmd-prompt">$ </span>git clone https://github.com/nextera-one/nexrun.git
<span class="cmd-prompt">$ </span>cd nexrun
<span class="cmd-prompt">$ </span>nexrun doctor
<span class="cmd-prompt">$ </span>nexrun validate -f examples/mysql/mysql.idel.yaml
<span class="cmd-prompt">$ </span>nexrun deploy -f examples/mysql/mysql.idel.yaml</code></pre>
              </div>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
        </section>

        <aside class="requirement-column" aria-label="Package requirements">
          <j-card class="requirement-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Runtime profile</span>
              <dl class="requirement-list">
                <div>
                  <dt><j-icon name="deployed_code" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Runtime</dt>
                  <dd>OCI / containerd</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt><j-icon name="speed" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>CPU</dt>
                  <dd>2,000 millicores</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt><j-icon name="memory" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Memory</dt>
                  <dd>2 GiB</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt><j-icon name="account_tree" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Processes</dt>
                  <dd>512</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt><j-icon name="lan" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Port</dt>
                  <dd>TCP 3306</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt><j-icon name="developer_board" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Architectures</dt>
                  <dd>AMD64, ARM64</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>

          <j-card class="requirement-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Instance configuration</span>
              <h2>2 volumes</h2>
              <p class="mono-item"><j-icon name="hard_drive" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><code>mysql-data</code></p>
              <p class="mono-item"><j-icon name="hard_drive" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><code>mysql-conf</code></p>
              <j-separator></j-separator>
              <h2>1 required secret</h2>
              <p class="mono-item"><j-icon name="key" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon><code>mysql-root-password</code></p>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>

          <j-card class="requirement-card requirement-card--links">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Source &amp; documentation</span>
              <a href="https://github.com/nextera-one/nexrun/tree/main/examples/mysql" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <j-icon name="code" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
                Kit source on GitHub
                <j-icon name="open_in_new" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
              </a>
              <a href="https://github.com/nextera-one/nexrun/blob/main/examples/mysql/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <j-icon name="menu_book" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
                MySQL kit README
                <j-icon name="open_in_new" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
              </a>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>

          <j-card class="requirement-card requirement-card--warning">
            <j-card-section>
              <j-icon name="warning" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
              <h2>Production note</h2>
              <p>Single-node MySQL is not database HA. Host loss causes downtime until the fenced volume is recovered or restored.</p>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </main>
  </j-page>
</template>
